From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 15:53:46 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] viz: a Direct3D 11 compositor for feature level 9_3 (Windows
 10 Mobile)

"The CPU draws, the GPU composites", as gecko-w10m does on the phones
whose GPU stops at Direct3D feature level 9_3, where ANGLE's Direct3D 11
backend cannot run. W10mD3D11Renderer is a SoftwareRenderer that draws
the frames it can with Direct3D 11, straight into the embedder's swap
chain: cc's CPU-rastered tiles and the other software resources become
BGRA textures once (cached by resource, evicted when viz lets the
resource go, within a budget of a few screens), and a frame is a clear
and one draw per quad with six level_9_3 shaders compiled offline with
fxc (w10m_d3d11_shaders.py regenerates the header).

In this version a GPU frame is one render pass of solid colour, tile and
texture quads, scaled and translated, clipped on the CPU, with opacity
and source-over blending; edges are placed where Skia would place them.
Any other frame -- more passes, filters, masks, rounded corners,
rotation, a copy request -- is drawn whole by the unmodified
SoftwareRenderer in the same DrawFrame, so nothing is ever missing from
the picture. Every ten seconds of animation the log says how many frames
went which way and why.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
